    "q-129666": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129666",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nI. $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n\nII. $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nIII. $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,1]$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14257924/assets/78af77d697ea292385e2bd2570c8185c728f57cc70c3edcc25ecccd0e84780e8.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles II and III do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle I cover the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
