    "q-129784": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129784",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14257924/assets/c54c756568a5f20d1d82a228c333dc4253a82236060ab2a7aea6260b10612140.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{3}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-4,3]\\times [-2,3]$\n\nII. ${∬}_{R}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,3]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-2,4]$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{3}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
