    "q-129895": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129895",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed between the curve $y=|x|-1$ and the line $y=2.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}xy{e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}xy{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-1,2]$\n\nII. ${∬}_{R}xy{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-1,3]$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}xy{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [0,3]$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14257924/assets/09707ef0347a6b67fc39c5247efbe19d22ca69b713738b5e3361cca5f965b021.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}xy{e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}xy{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
